<title>CANADA: Paperboard Q4 profit turns to loss.</title>
<headline>Paperboard Q4 profit turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			    1995</p>
<p> Shr   Loss		C$0.11     Loss	C$0.05</p>
<p> Net   Loss		 5,939   Profit	   828</p>
<p> Revs		     193,530		  232,098</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr   Profit	    C$0.28   Profit	C$0.61</p>
<p> Net   Profit	    13,753   Profit	31,662</p>
<p> Revs		     874,039		1,002,519</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Paperboard Industries Inc. Per share figures are fully diluted. Year earlier quarter and 12-month figures are restated. Latest fourth quarter net loss includes loss of C$7.5 million related to the sale of the European containerboard mill. Net earnings for the 1996 year include a non-recurring net loss after income taxes and noncontrolling interests of C$2.6 million, or C$0.06 a share.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
